ied\",\"detail\":\"12,482 findings checked; 2 carry this variant.\"},{\"label\":\"Evidence brief generated\",\"detail\":\"Composed from the structured fields of the cited records above.\"},{\"label\":\"Human review requested\",\"detail\":\"VariantPulse does not change any record. A clinician decides what happens next.\"}],\"caseId\":\"VP-R-2026-008\"},{\"variant\":{\"key\":\"HBB:c.380T>G\",\"gene\":\"HBB\",\"hgvsCoding\":\"c.380T>G\",\"proteinChange\":\"p.Val127Gly\",\"clinvarId\":\"15483\",\"recordedClassification\":\"PATHOGENIC\",\"recordedOn\":\"2023-01-30\",\"recordedEvidenceNote\":\"Reported as pathogenic following abnormal haemoglobin studies. Carrier status communicated for reproductive planning.\",\"condition\":\"Beta-thalassaemia / haemoglobinopathy\",\"panel\":\"Haemoglobinopathy panel\"},\"evidence\":{\"clinvarId\":\"15483\",\"accession\":\"VCV000015483\",\"title\":\"NM_000518.5(HBB):c.380T>G (p.Val127Gly)\",\"gene\":\"HBB\",\"cdnaChange\":\"c.380T>G\",\"variantType\":\"single nucleotide variant\",\"molecularConsequence\":\"missense variant\",\"proteinChange\":\"V127G\",\"rsid\":\"rs33925391\",\"classification\":\"Uncertain significance\",\"reviewStatus\":\"reviewed by expert panel\",\"lastEvaluated\":\"2026-04-30\",\"fdaRecognised\":true,\"submissionCount\":9,\"conditions\":[\"Beta-thalassemia HBB/LCRB\"],\"location\":{\"assembly\":\"GRCh38\",\"chr\":\"11\",\"band\":\"11p15.4\",\"start\":\"5225662\",\"stop\":\"5225662\"},\"peakAlleleFrequency\":null,\"citations\":[{\"pmid\":\"35543019\",\"title\":\"Strong Positive Dichlorophenolindophenol Precipitation Suggests Hb Dhonburi (or Hb Neapolis) (HBB: c.380T>G) Inheritance in a Couple at Risk for Severe β-Thalassemia.\",\"journal\":\"Hemoglobin\",\"year\":\"2022\"},{\"pmid\":\"31589614\",\"title\":\"Optimizing clinical exome design and parallel gene-testing for recessive genetic conditions in preconception carrier screening: Translational research genomic data from 14,125 exomes.\",\"journal\":\"PLoS Genet\",\"year\":\"2019\"},{\"pmid\":\"31240559\",\"title\":\"Molecular characteristics of thalassemia and hemoglobin variants in prenatal diagnosis program in northern Thailand.\",\"journal\":\"Int J Hematol\",\"year\":\"2019\"},{\"pmid\":\"28492532\",\"title\":\"Sherloc: a comprehensive refinement of the ACMG-AMP variant classification criteria.\",\"journal\":\"Genet Med\",\"year\":\"2017\"},{\"pmid\":\"28125089\",\"title\":\"Next-generation sequencing improves thalassemia carrier screening among premarital adults in a high prevalence population: the Dai nationality, China.\",\"journal\":\"Genet Med\",\"year\":\"2017\"},{\"pmid\":\"26467025\",\"title\":\"A Standardized DNA Variant Scoring System for Pathogenicity Assessments in Mendelian Disorders.\",\"journal\":\"Hum Mutat\",\"year\":\"2016\"},{\"pmid\":\"25052315\",\"title\":\"EMQN Best Practice Guidelines for molecular and haematology methods for carrier identification and prenatal diagnosis of the haemoglobinopathies.\",\"journal\":\"Eur J Hum Genet\",\"year\":\"2015\"},{\"pmid\":\"23525874\",\"title\":\"Problems in determining thalassemia carrier status in a program for prevention and control of severe thalassemia syndromes: a lesson from Thailand.\",\"journal\":\"Clin Chem Lab Med\",\"year\":\"2013\"}]},\"recordedCode\":\"PATHOGENIC\",\"currentCode\":\"VUS\",\"verdict\":{\"type\":\"CLASSIFICATION_DRIFT\",\"direction\":\"toward-benign\",\"rationale\":[\"Recorded interpretation normalised to Pathogenic.\",\"Current interpretation normalised to Uncertain significance.\",\"The interpretation left the clinically actionable band, so earlier management guidance may no longer apply.\"]},\"changeType\":\"REGIONAL_CONFLICT\",\"confidence\":{\"stars\":3,\"label\":\"Reviewed by expert panel\",\"strength\":\"Strong\"},\"regional\":{\"variantKey\":\"HBB:c.380T>G\",\"assertion\":\"PATHOGENIC\",\"observations\":0,\"cohortSize\":2884,\"regionalFrequency\":0,\"globalFrequency\":0.0000021,\"contributingCentres\":[\"Regional Haemoglobinopathy Network\",\"Premarital Screening Programme\"],\"lastUpdated\":\"2026-05-12\",\"note\":\"Global submitters downgraded this change to uncertain significance in April 2026. The regional index still carries the earlier pathogenic reading from haemoglobinopathy work-ups. Beta-thalassaemia carrier status is common in the UAE and drives premarital and reproductive counselling, so a disagreement here has direct family-planning consequences and must be resolved by a clinician, not by the software.\",\"citations\":[{\"pmid\":\"22074124\",\"title\":\"Molecular basis of β-thalassemia in the United Arab Emirates.\",\"journal\":\"Hemoglobin\",\"year\":\"2011\"},{\"pmid\":\"35330423\",\"title\":\"Middle Eastern Genetic Variation Improves Clinical Annotation of the Human Genome.\",\"journal\":\"J Pers Med\",\"year\":\"2022\"}]},\"regionalDisagreement\":{\"conflicting\":true,\"severity\":\"high\",\"reason\":\"One source places this variant in the clinically actionable band and the other does not.\",\"globalCode\":\"VUS\",\"regionalCode\":\"PATHOGENIC\"},\"impactedPatients\":[{\"id\":\"VP-10728\",\"ageBand\":\"25-34\",\"sex\":\"Female\",\"variantKey\":\"HBB:c.380T>G\",\"testedOn\":\"2023-01-30\",\"reportingLab\":\"Molecular Pathology Unit\",\"orderingDepartment\":\"Haematology\",\"clinicalOwner\":\"Dr. F. Al Mazrouei\",\"lastContact\":\"2023-02-22\",\"reviewState\":\"Not reviewed\",\"indication\":\"Premarital screening follow-up\"}],\"impactedRecordCount\":1,\"priority\":{\"level\":\"HIGH\",\"score\":90,\"factors\":[{\"label\":\"Moved out of the actionable band\",\"detail\":\"Pathogenic to Uncertain significance. Earlier guidance may no longer apply.\",\"weight\":45},{\"label\":\"Regional evidence conflicts\",\"detail\":\"Regional and global sources reach different conclusions.\",\"weight\":30},{\"label\":\"1 record on file\",\"detail\":\"Historical results carrying this variant that a reviewer would reassess.\",\"weight\":5},{\"label\":\"High review confidence\",\"detail\":\"The current classification carries expert-panel or guideline review.\",\"weight\":10}]},\"requiresReview\":true,\"summary\":\"Global and regional evidence disagree on HBB c.380T>G. The global consensus is uncertain significance, drawn from 9 submissions. The regional index asserts pathogenic on 0 observations across a cohort of 2,884. One source places this variant in the clinically actionable band and the other does not, which is the form of disagreement most likely to change a care decision. One record on file carries this variant and has not yet been reassessed.\",\"pipeline\":[{\"label\":\"Historical record retrieved\",\"detail\":\"HBB c.380T>G reported as Pathogenic on 2023-01-30.\"},{\"label\":\"Variant normalised\",\"detail\":\"Resolved to ClinVar VCV000015483 (rs33925391) and keyed as HBB:c.380T>G.\"},{\"label\":\"Current evidence retrieved\",\"detail\":\"Served from the bundled demo snapshot: Uncertain significance, 9 submissions, reviewed by expert panel.\"},{\"label\":\"Classification difference detected\",\"detail\":\"Recorded interpretation normalised to Pathogenic. Current interpretation normalised to Uncertain significance. The interpretation left the clinically actionable band, so earlier management guidance may no longer apply.\"},{\"label\":\"Regional sources compared\",\"detail\":\"Regional index asserts Pathogenic across 0 observations. One source places this variant in the clinically actionable band and the other does not.\"},{\"label\":\"Impacted records identified\",\"detail\":\"12,482 findings checked; 1 carries this variant.\"},{\"label\":\"Evidence brief generated\",\"detail\":\"Composed from the structured fields of the cited records above.\"},{\"label\":\"Human review requested\",\"detail\":\"VariantPulse does not change any record. A clinician decides what happens next.\"}],\"caseId\":\"VP-R-2026-002\"},{\"variant\":{\"key\":\"BRCA2:c.9538C>T\",\"gene\":\"BRCA2\",\"hgvsCoding\":\"c.9538C>T\",\"proteinChange\":\"p.Leu3180Phe\",\"clinvarId