",\"reviewStatus\":\"criteria provided, multiple submitters, no conflicts\",\"lastEvaluated\":\"2026-03-06\",\"fdaRecognised\":false,\"submissionCount\":23,\"conditions\":[\"Hemoglobin D disease\",\"beta Thalassemia\",\"Hereditary persistence of fetal hemoglobin\",\"Malaria, susceptibility to\",\"Hb SS disease\",\"Heinz body anemia\",\"Erythrocytosis, familial, 6\",\"Beta-thalassemia HBB/LCRB\",\"METHEMOGLOBINEMIA, BETA TYPE\",\"Dominant beta-thalassemia\",\"Hb SS disease\",\"HBB-related disorder\",\"Heinz body anemia\",\"Beta-thalassemia HBB/LCRB\"],\"location\":{\"assembly\":\"GRCh38\",\"chr\":\"11\",\"band\":\"11p15.4\",\"start\":\"5225678\",\"stop\":\"5225678\"},\"peakAlleleFrequency\":{\"value\":0.0006,\"source\":\"1000 Genomes Project\"},\"citations\":[{\"pmid\":\"33867742\",\"title\":\"Hb Brugg [HBA1:c.63C>A]: Report of an Ultra-Rare Variant Hemoglobin and Its Co-inheritance with Hb D-Punjab.\",\"journal\":\"Indian J Hematol Blood Transfus\",\"year\":\"2021\"},{\"pmid\":\"31973650\",\"title\":\"An Unusual Compound Heterozygosity for Hb O-Arab (HBB: c.364G>A) and Hb D-Los Angeles (HBB: c.364G>C).\",\"journal\":\"Hemoglobin\",\"year\":\"2020\"},{\"pmid\":\"31553106\",\"title\":\"Curating the gnomAD database: Report of novel variants in the globin-coding genes and bioinformatics analysis.\",\"journal\":\"Hum Mutat\",\"year\":\"2020\"},{\"pmid\":\"30626242\",\"title\":\"Rare Association of Hb D-Los Angeles (HBB: c.364G>C) with Hb H Disease: Diagnosis and Clinical Implications.\",\"journal\":\"Hemoglobin\",\"year\":\"2018\"},{\"pmid\":\"28492532\",\"title\":\"Sherloc: a comprehensive refinement of the ACMG-AMP variant classification criteria.\",\"journal\":\"Genet Med\",\"year\":\"2017\"},{\"pmid\":\"26467025\",\"title\":\"A Standardized DNA Variant Scoring System for Pathogenicity Assessments in Mendelian Disorders.\",\"journal\":\"Hum Mutat\",\"year\":\"2016\"},{\"pmid\":\"25818823\",\"title\":\"Hemoglobin D-Punjab: origin, distribution and laboratory diagnosis.\",\"journal\":\"Rev Bras Hematol Hemoter\",\"year\":\"2015\"},{\"pmid\":\"25741868\",\"title\":\"Standards and guidelines for the interpretation of sequence variants: a joint consensus recommendation of the American College of Medical Genetics and Genomics and the Association for Molecular Pathology.\",\"journal\":\"Genet Med\",\"year\":\"2015\"}]},\"recordedCode\":\"CONFLICTING\",\"currentCode\":\"PATHOGENIC\",\"verdict\":{\"type\":\"CLASSIFICATION_DRIFT\",\"direction\":\"none\",\"rationale\":[\"Recorded interpretation normalised to Conflicting classifications.\",\"Current interpretation normalised to Pathogenic.\",\"The interpretation crossed into the clinically actionable band, so records carrying it may need review.\"]},\"changeType\":\"CLASSIFICATION_DRIFT\",\"confidence\":{\"stars\":2,\"label\":\"Multiple submitters, no conflicts\",\"strength\":\"Moderate\"},\"regional\":{\"variantKey\":\"HBB:c.364G>C\",\"assertion\":\"PATHOGENIC\",\"observations\":11,\"cohortSize\":3031,\"regionalFrequency\":0.0018146,\"globalFrequency\":0.0004442,\"contributingCentres\":[\"CTGA, Centre for Arab Genomic Studies (UAE records)\"],\"lastUpdated\":\"2026-09-25\",\"note\":\"Haemoglobin D-Punjab. CTGA records it in UAE patients as likely pathogenic / pathogenic for sickle cell disease and beta-thalassaemia, and it is about four times more frequent in gnomAD's Middle Eastern group than globally. Global ClinVar submitters were still in conflict in January 2023 and only converged on pathogenic / likely pathogenic in March 2026: regional evidence was ahead of the global record.\",\"citations\":[{\"pmid\":\"22074124\",\"title\":\"Molecular basis of β-thalassemia in the United Arab Emirates.\",\"journal\":\"Hemoglobin\",\"year\":\"2011\"}]},\"regionalDisagreement\":{\"conflicting\":false,\"severity\":\"none\",\"reason\":\"Both sources place this variant in the same band.\",\"globalCode\":\"PATHOGENIC\",\"regionalCode\":\"PATHOGENIC\"},\"impactedPatients\":[{\"id\":\"VP-10701\",\"ageBand\":\"25-34\",\"sex\":\"Female\",\"variantKey\":\"HBB:c.364G>C\",\"testedOn\":\"2023-02-14\",\"reportingLab\":\"Molecular Pathology Unit\",\"orderingDepartment\":\"Haematology\",\"clinicalOwner\":\"Dr. F. Al Mazrouei\",\"lastContact\":\"2023-03-07\",\"reviewState\":\"Not reviewed\",\"indication\":\"Premarital screening follow-up\"},{\"id\":\"VP-10738\",\"ageBand\":\"5-11\",\"sex\":\"Male\",\"variantKey\":\"HBB:c.364G>C\",\"testedOn\":\"2023-06-05\",\"reportingLab\":\"Molecular Pathology Unit\",\"orderingDepartment\":\"Haematology\",\"clinicalOwner\":\"Dr. F. Al Mazrouei\",\"lastContact\":\"2024-01-22\",\"reviewState\":\"Not reviewed\",\"indication\":\"Anaemia work-up\"}],\"impactedRecordCount\":2,\"priority\":{\"level\":\"HIGH\",\"score\":70,\"factors\":[{\"label\":\"Moved into the actionable band\",\"detail\":\"Conflicting classifications to Pathogenic.\",\"weight\":60},{\"label\":\"2 records on file\",\"detail\":\"Historical results carrying this variant that a reviewer would reassess.\",\"weight\":10}]},\"requiresReview\":true,\"summary\":\"Since the 2023 report, the consensus for HBB c.364G>C has moved from conflicting classifications to pathogenic. That reading rests on 23 submissions at moderate review confidence, multiple submitters, no conflicts. That crosses the clinically actionable boundary, so management guidance issued on the original interpretation may no longer be the right guidance. 2 records on file carry this variant and have not yet been reassessed.\",\"pipeline\":[{\"label\":\"Historical record retrieved\",\"detail\":\"HBB c.364G>C reported as Conflicting classifications on 2023-02-14.\"},{\"label\":\"Variant normalised\",\"detail\":\"Resolved to ClinVar VCV000015152 (rs33946267) and keyed as HBB:c.364G>C.\"},{\"label\":\"Current evidence retrieved\",\"detail\":\"Served from the bundled demo snapshot: Pathogenic/Likely pathogenic, 23 submissions, criteria provided, multiple submitters, no conflicts.\"},{\"label\":\"Classification difference detected\",\"detail\":\"Recorded interpretation normalised to Conflicting classifications. Current interpretation normalised to Pathogenic. The interpretation crossed into the clinically actionable band, so records carrying it may need review.\"},{\"label\":\"Regional sources compared\",\"detail\":\"Regional index asserts Pathogenic, consistent with the global reading.\"},{\"label\":\"Impacted records identified\",\"detail\":\"12,482 findings checked; 2 carry this variant.\"},{\"label\":\"Evidence brief generated\",\"detail\":\"Composed from the structured fields of the cited records above.\"},{\"label\":\"Human review requested\",\"detail\":\"VariantPulse does not change any record. A clinician decides what happens next.\"}],\"caseId\":\"VP-R-2026-007\"},{\"variant\":{\"key\":\"MYBPC3:c.776delinsTT\",\"gene\":\"MYBPC3\",\"hgvsCoding\":\"c.776delinsTT\",\"proteinChange\":\"p.Ala259fs\",\"clinvarId\":\"4689837\",\"recordedClassification\":\"VUS\",\"recordedOn\":\"2023-03-20\",\"recordedEvidenceNote\":\"Novel frameshift change with no public submissions at the time of reporting. Classified as uncertain pending further evidence.\",\"condition\":\"Left ventricular non-compaction / cardiomyopathy\",\"panel\":\"Inherited cardiac conditions panel\"},\"evidence\":{\"clinvarId\":\"4689837\",\"accession\":\"VCV004689837\",\"title\":\"NM_000256.3(MYBPC3):c.776delinsTT (p.Ala259fs)\",\"gene\":\"MYBPC3\",\"cdnaChange\":\"c.776delinsTT\",\"variantType\":\"Indel\",\"molecularConsequence\":\"frameshift variant\",\"proteinChange\":\"A259fs\",\"rsid\":null,\"classification\":\"Likely pathogenic\",\"reviewStatus\":\"criteria provided, single submitter\",\"lastEvaluated\":\"2025-07-31\",\"fdaRecognised\":false,\"submissionCount\":1,\"conditions\":[],\"location\":{\"assembly\":\"GRCh38\",\"chr\":\"11\",\"band\":\"11p11.2\",\"start\":\"47347902\",\"stop\":\"47347902\"},\"peakAlleleFrequency\":null,\"citations\":[]},\"recordedCode\":\"VUS\",\"currentCode\":\"LIKELY_PATHOGENIC\",\"verdict\":{\"type\":\"CLASSIFICATION_DRIFT\",\"direction\":\"toward-pathogenic\",\"rationale\":[\"Recorded interpretation normalised to Uncertain significance.\",\"Current interpretation normalised to Likely pathogenic.\",\"The interpretation crossed into the clinically actionable band, so records carrying it may need review.\"]},\"changeType\":\"CLASSIFICATION_DRIFT\",\"confidence\":{\"stars\":1,\"label\":\"Single submitter\",\"strength\":\"Limited\"},\"regional\":{\"variantKey\":\"MYBPC3:c.776delinsTT\",\"assertion\":\"LIKELY_PATHOGENIC\",\"observations\":0,\"cohortSize\":3042,\"regionalFrequency\":0,\"globalFrequency\":0,\"contributingCentres\":[\"CTGA, Centre for Arab Genomic Studies (UAE records)\"],\"lastUpdated\":\"2026-09-25\",\"note\":\"CTGA lists this frameshift in a UAE patient as likely pathogenic for left ventricular non-compaction (record dated 2020). It did not appear in ClinVar until after January 2023 (first classified likely pathogenic, July 2025, single submitter). Another case where a regional catalogue carried the answer before global databases did.\",\"citations\":[]},\"regionalDisagreement\":{\"conflicting\":false,\"severity\":\"none\",\"reason\":\"Both sources place this variant in the same band.\",\"globalCode\":\"LIKELY_PATHOGENIC\",\"regionalCode\":\"LIKELY_PATHOGENIC\"},\"impactedPatients\":[{\"id\":\"VP-10775\",\"ageBand\":\"35-44\",\"sex\":\"Male\",\"variantKey\":\"MYBPC3:c.776delinsTT\",\"testedOn\":\"2023-03-20\",\"reportingLab\":\"Cardiac Genetics Laboratory\",\"orderingDepartment\":\"Cardiology\",\"clinicalOwner\":\"Dr. P. Varga\",\"lastContact\":\"2024-06-11\",\"reviewState\":\"Not reviewed\",\"indication\":\"Cardiomyopathy on imaging\"},{\"id\":\"VP-10812\",\"ageBand\":\"12-17\",\"sex\":\"Female\",\"variantKey\":\"MYBPC3:c.776delinsTT\",\"testedOn\":\"2023-07-17\",\"reportingLab\":\"Cardiac Genetics Laboratory\",\"orderingDepartment\":\"Cardiology\",\"clinicalOwner\":\"Dr. P. Varga\",\"lastContact\":\"2023-09-04\",\"reviewState\":\"Not reviewed\",\"indication\":\"Cascade testing following a family result\"}],\"impactedRecordCount\":2,\"priority\":{\"level\":\"HIGH\",\"score\":65,\"factors\":[{\"label\":\"Moved into the actionable band\",\"detail\":\"Uncertain significance to Likely pathogenic.\",\"weight\":60},{\"label\":\"2 records on file\",\"detail\":\"Historical results carrying this variant that a reviewer would reassess.\",\"weight\":10},{\"label\":\"Limited review confidence\",\"detail\":\"The current classification rests on a narrow submission base.\",\"weight\":-5}]},\"requiresReview\":true,\"summary\":\"Since the 2023 report, the consensus for MYBPC3 c.776delinsTT has moved from uncertain significance to likely pathogenic. That reading rests on a single submission at limited review confidence, single submitter. That crosses the clinically actionable boundary, so management guidance issued on the original interpretation may no longer be the right guidance. 2 records on file carry this variant and have not yet been reassessed.\",\"pipeline\":[{\"label\":\"Historical record retrieved\",\"detail\":\"MYBPC3 c.776delinsTT reported as Uncertain significance on 2023-03-20.\"},{\"label\":\"Variant normalised\",\"detail\":\"Resolved to ClinVar VCV004689837 and keyed as MYBPC3:c.776delinsTT.\"},{\"label\":\"Current evidence retrieved\",\"detail\":\"Served from the bundled demo snapshot: Likely pathogenic, 1 submission, criteria provided, single submitter.\"},{\"label\":\"Classification difference detected\",\"detail\":\"Recorded interpretation normalised to Uncertain significance. Current interpretation normalised to Likely pathogenic. The interpretation crossed into the clinically actionable band, so records carrying it may need review.\"},{\"label\":\"Regional sources compared\",\"detail\":\"Regional index asserts Likely pathogenic, consistent with the global reading.\"},{\"label\":\"Impacted records identified\",\"detail\":\"12,482 findings checked; 2 carry this variant.\"},{\"label\":\"Evidence brief generated\",\"detail\":\"Composed from the structured fields of the cited records above.\"},{\"label\":\"Human review requested\",\"detail\":\"VariantPulse does not change any record. A clinician decides what happens next.\"}],\"caseId\":\"VP-R-2026-009\"},{\"variant\":{\"key\":\"BRCA1:c.1140dup\",\"gene\":\"BRCA1\",\"hgvsCoding\":\"c.1140dup\",\"proteinChange\":\"p.Lys381fs\",\"clinvarId\":\"231732\",\"recordedClassification\":\"PATHOGENIC\",\"recordedOn\":\"2022-10-03\",\"recordedEvidenceNote\":\"Frameshift change reported as pathogenic by expert-panel criteria. Surveillance and cascade testing offered.\",\"condition\":\"Hereditary breast and ovarian cancer\",\"panel\":\"Hereditary cancer panel\"},\"evidence\":{\"clinvarId\":\"231732\",\"accession\":\"VCV000231732\",\"title\":\"NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.1140dup (p.Lys381fs)\",\"gene\":\"BRCA1\",\"cdnaChange\":\"c.1140dup\",\"variantType\":\"Duplication\",\"molecularConsequence\":\"frameshift variant\",\"proteinChange\":\"K334fs\",\"rsid\":\"rs876659327\",\"classification\":\"Pathogenic\",\"reviewStatus\":\"reviewed by expert panel\",\"lastEvaluated\":\"2017-12-15\",\"fdaRecognised\":false,\"submissionCount\":12,\"conditions\":[\"Breast-ovarian cancer, familial, susceptibility to, 1\"],\"location\":{\"assembly\":\"GRCh38\",\"chr\":\"17\",\"band\":\"17q21.31\",\"start\":\"43094390\",\"stop\":\"43094391\"},\"peakAlleleFrequency\":null,\"citations\":[{\"pmid\":\"42258614\",\"title\":\"ATM-Related Cancer Predisposition.\",\"journal\":\"University of Washington, Seattle\",\"year\":\"1993\"},{\"pmid\":\"35802134\",\"title\":\"ACMG SF v3.1 list for reporting of secondary findings in clinical exome and genome sequencing: A policy statement of the American College of Medical Genetics and Genomics (ACMG).\",\"journal\":\"Genet Med\",\"year\":\"2022\"},{\"pmid\":\"34980015\",\"title\":\"Assessing frequency and clinical outcomes of BRCA mutated ovarian cancer in Saudi women.\",\"journal\":\"BMC Cancer\",\"year\":\"2022\"},{\"pmid\":\"34242744\",\"title\":\"Customizing local and systemic therapies for women with early breast cancer: the St. Gallen International Consensus Guidelines for treatment of early breast cancer 2021.\",\"journal\":\"Ann Oncol\",\"year\":\"2021\"},{\"pmid\":\"34012068\",\"title\":\"ACMG SF v3.0 list for reporting of secondary findings in clinical exome and genome sequencing: a policy statement of the American College of Medical Genetics and Genomics (ACMG).\",\"journal\":\"Genet Med\",\"year\":\"2021\"},{\"pmid\":\"33410258\",\"title\":\"Risk assessment and genetic counseling for hereditary breast and ovarian cancer syndromes-Practice resource of the National Society of Genetic Counselors.\",\"journal\":\"J Genet Couns\",\"year\":\"2021\"},{\"pmid\":\"31479213\",\"title\":\"Risk Assessment, Genetic Counseling, and Genetic Testing for BRCA1/2-Related Cancer in Women: A Systematic Review for the U.S. Preventive Services Task Force\",\"journal\":\"Agency for Healthcare Research and Quality (US)\",\"year\":\"2019\"},{\"pmid\":\"31429903\",\"title\":\"Risk Assessment, Genetic Counseling, and Genetic Testing for BRCA-Related Cancer: US Preventive Services Task Force Recommendation Statement.\",\"journal\":\"JAMA\",\"year\":\"2019\"}]},\"recordedCode\":\"PATHOGENIC\",\"currentCode\":\"PATHOGENIC\",\"verdict\":{\"type\":\"NO_MATERIAL_CHANGE\",\"direction\":\"none\",\"rationale\":[\"Recorded interpretation normalised to Pathogenic.\",\"Current interpretation normalised to Pathogenic.\",\"Codes are identical, so no reclassification has occurred.\"]},\"changeType\":\"NO_MATERIAL_CHANGE\",\"confidence\":{\"stars\":3,\"label\":\"Reviewed by expert panel\",\"strength\":\"Strong\"},\"regional\":{\"variantKey\":\"BRCA1:c.1140dup\",\"assertion\":\"PATHOGENIC\",\"observations\":0,\"cohortSize\":3042,\"regionalFrequency\":0,\"globalFrequency\":0,\"contributingCentres\":[\"CTGA, Centre for Arab Genomic Studies (UAE and Yemen records)\"],\"lastUpdated\":\"2026-09-25\",\"note\":\"CTGA records this frameshift in a UAE family (Rawashdeh et al. 2024) and a Yemeni patient (Al-Ali et al. 2023). Regional and global readings agree: pathogenic. Included as a control, so the system shows it does not raise an alert when nothing has changed.\",\"citations\":[]},\"regionalDisagreement\":{\"conflicting\":false,\"severity\":\"none\",\"reason\":\"Both sources place this variant in the same band.\",\"globalCode\":\"PATHOGENIC\",\"regionalCode\":\"PATHOGENIC\"},\"impactedPatients\":[{\"id\":\"VP-10849\",\"ageBand\":\"45-54\",\"sex\":\"Female\",\"variantKey\":\"BRCA1:c.1140dup\",\"testedOn\":\"2022-10-03\",\"reportingLab\":\"Genomics Core Laboratory\",\"orderingDepartment\":\"Clinical Genetics\",\"clinicalOwner\":\"Dr. L. Haddad\",\"lastContact\":\"2024-10-15\",\"reviewState\":\"Closed\",\"indication\":\"Family history of breast cancer\"}],\"impactedRecordCount\":1,\"priority\":{\"level\":\"LOW\",\"score\":15,\"factors\":[{\"label\":\"1 record on file\",\"detail\":\"Historical results carrying this variant that a reviewer would reassess.\",\"weight\":5},{\"label\":\"High review confidence\",\"detail\":\"The current classification carries expert-panel or guideline review.\",\"weight\":10}]},\"requiresReview\":false,\"summary\":\"Current evidence for BRCA1 c.1140dup agrees with the pathogenic interpretation issued in 2022. The classification was last evaluated on 15 Dec 2017 and carries 12 submissions.\",\"pipeline\":[{\"label\":\"Historical record retrieved\",\"detail\":\"BRCA1 c.1140dup reported as Pathogenic on 2022-10-03.\"},{\"label\":\"Variant normalised\",\"detail\":\"Resolved to ClinVar VCV000231732 (rs876659327) and keyed as BRCA1:c.1140dup.\"},{\"label\":\"Current evidence retrieved\",\"detail\":\"Served from the bundled demo snapshot: Pathogenic, 12 submissions, reviewed by expert panel.\"},{\"label\":\"Classification difference detected\",\"detail\":\"Recorded interpretation normalised to Pathogenic. Current interpretation normalised to Pathogenic. Codes are identical, so no reclassification has occurred.\"},{\"label\":\"Regional sources compared\",\"detail\":\"Regional index asserts Pathogenic, consistent with the global reading.\"},{\"label\":\"Impacted records identified\",\"detail\":\"12,482 findings checked; 1 carries this variant.\"},{\"label\":\"Evidence brief generated\",\"detail\":\"Composed from the structured fields of the cited records above.\"},{\"label\":\"Human review requested\",\"detail\":\"VariantPulse does not change any record. A clinician decides what happens next.\"}],\"caseId\":null}],\"changeKeys\":[\"BRCA1:c.5056C>T\",\"BRCA2:c.7847C>T\",\"TP53:c.589G>A\",\"LDLR:c.1381G>T\",\"PTEN:c.149T>C\",\"HBB:c.364G>C\",\"MYBPC3:c.26-2A>G\",\"MYBPC3:c.776delinsTT\",\"BRCA2:c.9538C>T\",\"TP53:c.784G>A\"],\"regionalConflictKeys\":[\"HBB:c.380T>G\",\"CFTR:c.601G>A\"],\"reviewableKeys\":[\"BRCA1:c.5056C>T\",\"HBB:c.380T>G\",\"BRCA2:c.7847C>T\",\"TP53:c.589G>A\",\"LDLR:c.1381G>T\",\"PTEN:c.149T>C\",\"HBB:c.364G>C\",\"MYBPC3:c.26-2A>G\",\"MYBPC3:c.776delinsTT\",\"CFTR:c.601G>A\",\"BRCA1:c.5123C>T\",\"BRCA2:c.9538C>T\",\"TP53:c.784G>A\"]},\"children\":[\"$L1a\",\"$L1b\",\"$L1c\"]}]}]}]\n1d:I[671,[\"986\",\"static/chunks/986-8ebe740d18273266.js\",\"619\",\"static/chunks/619-ba102abea3e3d0e4.js\",\"360\",\"static/chunks/360-fc8f704cc41c8957.js\",\"307\",\"static/chunks/307-735417e0d45b0209.js\",\"771\",\"static/chunks/771-abf0a596fc78642a.js\",\"177\",\"static/chunks/app/layout-fe0a05b41efa28c2.js\"],\"Sidebar\"]\n1e:I[8903,[\"986\",\"static/chunks/986-8ebe740d18273266.js\",\"619\",\"static/chunks/619-ba102abea3e3d0e4.js\",\"360\",\"static/chunks/360-fc8f704cc41c8957.js\",\"307\",\"static/chunks/307-735417e0d45b0209.js\",\"771\",\"static/chunks/771-abf0a596fc78642a.js\",\"177\",\"static/chunks/app/layout-fe0a05b41efa28c2.js\"],\"Topbar\"]\n1f:I[960,[\"986\",\"static/chunks/986-8ebe740d18273266.js\",\"307\",\"static/chunks/307-735417e0d45b0209.js\",\"39\",\"static/chunks/app/error-be59cc9fe6d263a9.js\"],\"default\"]\n20